    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d517">

                <pb facs="0530" n="524" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg524"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.01/848</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Assistant Secretary
                        of State (Berle)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-06-11">June 11, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>M. Tixier came in to see me today. He presented a note dated June 11, 1942<anchor
                        n="53" xml:id="d517-f1"/> referring to his note of May 18.<anchor n="54"
                        xml:id="d517-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>He said that he hoped we would study the note and thereafter discuss it with him
                    orally. His personal view was that the note should not be the foundation for an
                    exchange of notes. (Having glanced at it, I fully agree with M. Tixier.)</p>
                <p>The note is, in brief, a protest against our “neutralization” of the French
                    colonies in the New World and an insistence that what we are really doing is
                    creating a third French government, namely, the government of Admiral Robert.
                    The note then wanders on to a statement that unless we turn over these various
                    colonies to the Free French we diminish their effectiveness in the war effort
                    and their usefulness in the ultimate reorganization of France.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>A. A. B[<hi rendition="#small-caps">erle</hi>], <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">Jr.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
